H("889.d.1.B",4,"A two-person engine hoist job goes smoothly when each person:","knows their role and communicates clearly",["works silently","guesses","avoids the other"],"Clear roles.")
H("889.d.1.C",3,"A powerplant student learns that a technician must never sign for work on a magneto that she did not personally verify. She is identifying:","individual ethical and legal behavior standards according to professional and industry standards",["no standards","optional rules","shop humor"],"Legal conduct.")
H("889.d.1.C",4,"Signing a logbook entry for work you did not do is:","a violation of ethical and legal standards",["acceptable","a shortcut","common practice"],"False sign-off.")
H("889.d.1.D",3,"A class researches why engine maintenance manuals and service bulletins are in English and why technicians must read them accurately. They are discussing:","the impact of English language proficiency requirements on aviation",["no impact","a local custom","a style choice"],"English requirement.")
H("889.d.1.D",4,"A misread torque value in an engine manual could lead to:","a loose or overstressed fastener",["a perfect assembly","a faster job","an easier repair"],"Misread data.")
H("889.d.1.E",3,"A shop talk covers fatigue, distraction, stress and rushing as causes of errors in engine work. They are identifying:","human factors that may impact health and safety in a worksite",["no factors","weather factors","tool brands"],"Human factors.")
H("889.d.1.E",4,"Working a double shift without rest increases the risk of:","mistakes and injury",["better focus","fewer errors","extra safety"],"Fatigue.")
H("889.d.1.F",3,"A lead requires a second technician to inspect a safety-wired propeller bolt, because even experts miss things. This explains:","the role of human factors in maintaining health and safety in the workplace",["no role","tool failure","paint issues"],"Error checks.")
H("889.d.1.F",4,"Checklists and independent inspections are used mainly to:","catch errors caused by human factors",["slow the work","avoid training","hide mistakes"],"Safeguards.")
H("889.d.1.G",3,"A technician stops a job when she realizes she skipped a step, even though the plane is due out in an hour. This shows how:","an employee's personal responsibility attitudes can affect health and safety",["pressure removes responsibility","safety is optional","schedules come first"],"Own the stop.")
H("889.d.1.G",4,"A responsible technician who finds her own error should:","report it and correct it before release",["hide it","wait to see","blame someone"],"Admit errors.")
H("889.d.1.H",3,"In a role-play, a customer asks a student to sign off an engine run-up that was never done. The student refuses and explains why. She is applying:","reasoning skills to simulated workplace situations in order to make ethical decisions",["poor judgment","rule breaking","avoidance"],"Ethics role-play.")
H("889.d.1.H",4,"When asked to falsify a record, an ethical technician should:","decline and document the request",["comply","ignore it","accept payment"],"Say no.")
